🎉 Summary: What We've Achieved
🏗️ Complete Multi-Tenant SaaS Platform with Role-Based Access Control

1️⃣ User Management System ✅
Four User Roles:

SUPER_ADMIN - Platform owner (you)
CLIENT_ADMIN - Your customers (pay you)
DEVELOPER - Employees of CLIENT_ADMIN
END_USER - Customers of CLIENT_ADMIN's websites

Invitation System:

CLIENT_ADMIN can invite DEVELOPERS
Developers accept invitation via email link
Separate auth flows for platform vs website users


2️⃣ Two-Tier Access Control ✅
Organization-Level Control (SUPER_ADMIN):
SUPER_ADMIN → Controls Organizations
    ↓
Organization.status = INACTIVE
    ↓
Locks ENTIRE organization:
  ✓ Admin panel blocked
  ✓ All projects inaccessible
  ✓ All users locked out
  ✓ Instant reactivation
Project-Level Control (CLIENT_ADMIN):
CLIENT_ADMIN → Controls Individual Projects
    ↓
Project.projectStatus = INACTIVE
    ↓
Locks ONLY this project:
  ✓ Public website shows "unavailable"
  ✓ END_USERs can't access
  ✓ Other projects still work
  ✓ Toggle ON/OFF anytime

3️⃣ Security & Permissions ✅
Role-Based Permissions:
ActionSUPER_ADMINCLIENT_ADMINDEVELOPEREND_USERToggle Organization✅❌❌❌Toggle Project✅✅ Own org❌❌Create Project✅✅ Within limit✅ Within limit❌Edit Project✅✅ Own org✅ Own org❌Delete Project✅✅ Own org✅ Own org❌View Templates✅✅✅❌Clone Template✅✅✅❌Invite Developers❌✅❌❌Manage Users✅ All✅ Own team❌❌
Data Isolation:

✅ Organizations cannot see each other's data
✅ Cross-organization access blocked
✅ API configs scoped to organization
✅ Dynamic entities scoped to organization
✅ Global resources (templates) accessible to all


4️⃣ Project Management ✅
Features Implemented:

✅ Project Limits - Based on pricing plan (4/8/10 projects)
✅ Project Status Toggle - Turn websites ON/OFF instantly
✅ Template System - Global starter templates by SUPER_ADMIN
✅ Clone Templates - One-click project creation
✅ Project Visibility - Templates + own org's projects
✅ Status Indicators - Visual badges (Active/Inactive/Maintenance)

Frontend Table Features:
ColumnDescriptionTitleProject name with template badgeSlugURL-friendly identifierOrganizationWhich org owns itPublish StatusDraft/Active/DeletedProject StatusACTIVE/INACTIVE (NEW)AnonymousToggle authenticationAccess SwitchON/OFF toggle (NEW)ActionsEdit/Delete/Clone

5️⃣ Authentication System ✅
Platform Login (/api/auth/login):

SUPER_ADMIN, CLIENT_ADMIN, DEVELOPER
Email verification required
Payment verification (CLIENT_ADMIN only)
Organization status check
JWT token in HTTP-only cookie

Website Login (/api/enduser-auth/login):

END_USER, END_USER_ADMIN
Separate authentication flow
No payment required
Per-website JWT cookies
Independent from platform status

Fixed Issues:

✅ Organization status check (not billing.status)
✅ Safe property access
✅ All roles can now login successfully


6️⃣ Dynamic CRUD System ✅
Global Entity Support:

✅ SUPER_ADMIN creates global entities (all orgs can use)
✅ CLIENT_ADMIN creates org-specific entities
✅ Permission-based access control
✅ Read-only global entities for non-admins

Features:

✅ Dynamic entity creation
✅ Role-based filtering (global + own org)
✅ CRUD operations with permissions
✅ File upload support
✅ Pagination & search


7️⃣ API Configuration System ✅
Security:

✅ Global APIs visible to all
✅ Org-specific APIs isolated
✅ Permission checks on all operations
✅ No cross-organization access


8️⃣ Key Architecture Decisions ✅
Why Organization/Project-Level vs User-Level:
AspectUser DeactivationOrg/Project DeactivationComplexityHigh (cascade)Low (status check)PerformanceSlow (100+ DB updates)Fast (1 DB update)ReactivationComplex restoreInstant toggleCodeHard to maintainSimple middlewareIndustryNot standardUsed by AWS, Heroku
Correct Hierarchy:
SUPER_ADMIN pays platform fees
    ↓
CLIENT_ADMIN (your customer)
    ↓ pays subscription to SUPER_ADMIN
Controls their organization + projects
    ↓
DEVELOPER (employee of CLIENT_ADMIN)
    ↓ builds websites
END_USER_ADMIN (CLIENT_ADMIN's customer)
    ↓ pays CLIENT_ADMIN (not you!)
END_USER (end customers)

🎯 Business Logic:
When CLIENT_ADMIN doesn't pay SUPER_ADMIN:
SUPER_ADMIN → Deactivate Organization
    ↓
✅ Organization.status = INACTIVE
    ↓
Effects:
  - Admin panel locked for CLIENT_ADMIN
  - Developers can't access
  - All projects inaccessible
  - END_USERs can't access websites
    ↓
BUT: No user records changed, instant reactivation
When END_USER_ADMIN doesn't pay CLIENT_ADMIN:
CLIENT_ADMIN → Deactivate Project
    ↓
✅ Project.projectStatus = INACTIVE
    ↓
Effects:
  - Only THIS project locked
  - END_USERs see "unavailable" message
  - Other projects still work
    ↓
CLIENT_ADMIN decides, not SUPER_ADMIN